---
// Goal: show full detailed output and link to the normative result contract.
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Terminal from '../../../components/Terminal.astro';
import Code from '../../../components/Code.astro';
import { captioned } from '../../../data/samples.mjs';
import { REPO } from '../../../data/catalog.mjs';
import wire from '../../../../recordings/6c7bf37d01fcf7003f7bd8f216e0a3b84dd5d47a52ebe80fb1a4ca69180cc83b.json';

const see = {
  decide: 'A yes answer with its probability and run fields.',
  find: 'The selected unit and the probabilities for every unit.',
  score: 'The weighted position and probabilities for each level.',
  tag: 'The labels that cleared the cut and all label probabilities.',
};
const runs = captioned('reference/details', see);
---
<Base title="Detailed results" description="Full ThinkThen detailed outputs and their result fields.">
  <h1>Detailed results</h1>
  <p class="lede"><code>--details</code> replaces a bare value with the complete result. The <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/specification/result.md`}>result contract</a> fixes its exact shape and failure cases.</p>
  <p>The command writes one complete <code>thinkthen.result/1</code> JSON object per row. It includes the answer, its probabilities, the resolved rule, and run metadata. A recorded or cached answer reports zero requests sent for that call.</p>
  <p><a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/specification/types.md`}>Answer types</a> keep <code>null</code> for not sure distinct from a failure. The <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/specification/result.schema.json`}>result schema</a> checks the JSON shape; the result contract also fixes semantic rules and field order. An <code>annotate</code> member that fails carries a separate <code>failed</code> marker.</p>
  <p>Read <code>answer.kind</code> before a probability: <code>yes_no</code> has one <code>probability</code>; <code>choice</code> has a <code>pick</code> and probabilities keyed by option; <code>score</code> has level probabilities while <code>value</code> is the weighted number. The <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/specification/result.md`}>result contract</a> defines <code>tag</code> and <code>find</code> too, plus the aggregate recognize and relate shapes.</p>
  <p>Call failures have the six stable kinds <code>usage</code>, <code>backend</code>, <code>deadline</code>, <code>local</code>, <code>cancelled</code>, and <code>defect</code>. The <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/specification/types.md`}>type contract</a> defines their native carriers. An error message is advice, not an identifier; the C ABI alone assigns numeric codes 1–6.</p>

  <h2>One recorded HTTP body pair</h2>
  <p>The <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/site/recordings/6c7bf37d01fcf7003f7bd8f216e0a3b84dd5d47a52ebe80fb1a4ca69180cc83b.json`}>saved exchange</a> has the exact request and Jev response bodies. Recordings omit headers, including the key. Here the backend reports <code>usage</code>; the result's <code>meta.usage</code> carries those token counts.</p>
  <Code code={`POST ${wire.url}\n${JSON.stringify(wire.request, null, 2)}`} caption="Request body" copy={false} />
  <Code code={JSON.stringify(wire.response, null, 2)} caption="Response body" copy={false} />

  <h2>Full examples</h2>
  {runs.map((run) => <Terminal run={run} caption={run.see} />)}
</Base>
